{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"jaunty-pugnacious-stinkpot","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Context / Problem\n\nNine real scanner integration tests skip when binaries are absent at `tests/unit/test_code_review_conflict_markers.py:97-158`, `test_code_review_public_exposure.py:109-151`, and `test_code_review_ws5.py:347-399`. Verified installs neither scanner although `infra/compose/Dockerfile.reviewbot:43-71` makes them runtime prerequisites.\n\n## Approach\n\nCreate one checked-in scanner lock manifest consumed by the review-bot image and CI provisioning. Pin Semgrep and Gitleaks versions plus artifact hashes. Add a native-binary Make target that fails on missing/wrong binaries and runs the focused integration tests. Invoke it from a reusable parallel workflow used by mirror CI and the exact-patchset Gerrit lane, and include that job in `vote.needs`.\n\nDo not build Docker, install OpenGrep, or add this target to normal `make lint`/default local tests.\n\n## Scope\n\n- scanner version manifest and review-bot Dockerfile\n- provisioning helper and explicit Make target\n- scanner integration tests\n- reusable mirror/Gerrit workflow and Verified parity guard\n\n## Testing\n\nProve missing binary, wrong version/hash, valid Semgrep rule, and valid Gitleaks secret/SARIF behavior. Exercise workflow wiring and `vote.needs` parity structurally.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] Semgrep and Gitleaks versions and downloadable artifact hashes are single-sourced and consumed by deployment plus CI.\n- [ ] The explicit native-binary target fails for missing or wrong scanners and passes the nine real integration contracts.\n- [ ] One parallel reusable lane serves mirror CI and exact Gerrit patchsets and is required by the Verified vote.\n- [ ] OpenGrep, Docker-image builds, normal `make lint`, and default local tests remain outside scope.\n- [ ] The lane's expected cold-run cost is documented as approximately 1.5-3 runner-minutes without extending the existing 22-23 minute critical path when capacity is available.","id":"aa9e-3d35-fd3e-41ee","parent_id":"78f2-b104-e3c9-4b86","priority":1,"tags":["janitor","ci","security","rp14"],"ticket_type":"story","title":"Run pinned deployed Semgrep and Gitleaks contracts in Verified"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1788311614552960001,"uuid":"94b2a2f1-fe2a-48b8-94fe-903151a980e9"}